+// GeneralsX @feature Zero Hour Reforged 11/11/2026 (M2 wave 6, slice 6d): the bounded catch-up
+// contract, named as Reforged names it (their GameEngine.h).  The GX catch-up below already
+// implements this contract -- a wall-clock debt window of LOGIC_CATCHUP_MAX_MS and a per-pass
+// budget of LOGIC_CATCHUP_BUDGET_MS -- and v1.4 only names the constants and wires the literals
+// to them; no pacing decision changes.  The host's own caps stay deliberately tighter than
+// upstream's frame-count cap (at most 3 extra steps per pass, residual debt clamped to one
+// frame): on this hardware the 8 ms budget binds first, and past the caps the surplus is
+// dropped so the game runs honestly slow rather than spiralling.  The frames-of-debt form of
+// the cap (debt window x logic rate) is what the converted-rate build will consume.
+static const Real LOGIC_CATCHUP_MAX_MS = 100.0f;
+static const Real LOGIC_CATCHUP_BUDGET_MS = 8.0f;
